---
source: tests/cli_help_snapshot_tests.rs
description: gpy-agent --help
expression: result.stdout
---
Fast, cross-platform agent for Git status and language detection used by the GPY prompt for Bash, Fish, and Zsh

Usage: gpy-agent <COMMAND>

Commands:
  start    Start the agent as a background process
  stop     Stop the background agent process
  status   Show the current status of the agent
  theme    Theme management commands
  palette  Palette (color theme) management commands
  oneshot  Run a single command and print the result (used as a fallback)
  config   Query configuration values from config.toml (used by shell integrations)
  doctor   Run system diagnostics to check for common issues
  init     Bootstrap configuration on first install (picks a Nerd/ASCII icon default that renders on this machine). No-op when a config file already exists
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
